{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Talking About the Future", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "That's Just Silly Talk", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 14, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future Continuous tense to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future.<br/>You use the Future Perfect tense to talk about an action in the future before another action in the future. This is the past in the future. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> tense, the action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">I will be studying at the library at 4 p.m. tomorrow. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The person will start studying at some point in the future and be studying at 4 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop studying. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span>, you can sometimes think of the Future Perfect tense like the Present Perfect tense, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">You can call me at work at 8 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have arrived</span> at the office by 8.  <br/>The train will leave the station at 9 a.m. You will arrive at the station at 9:15 a.m. When you arrive, the train <span class=\"strong\">will have left</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for the structure of the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> (<span class=\\\"italic\\\">not</span>) + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">be</span> + verb <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will</span> you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">be heading</span> back to work tomorrow?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">In five years, I<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'ll have saved</span> enough money to buy a house. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I'll have paid for almost half of the trip by the end of the month.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll have saved enough money to buy a house. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Before that happens I'll have started my own PR company. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Will you be heading back to work tomorrow?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll be blogging!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Talking About Future Actions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about a things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the Simple Present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong italic\\\">Will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I will also stop squandering my money. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong italic\\\">Be going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Basically for the next two years I am going to spend as little money as possible.  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Peter's picking us up soon. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It opens at 8:30.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I am putting in at least 60 hours at the restaurant this week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will also stop squandering my money. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's going to be a challenge.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am starting a retirement fund as soon as I pay off the trip. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I meet with someone at the bank tomorrow before work. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It opens at 8:30 and I have the first appointment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You guys will be fine.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to keep up to date", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to provide the latest information to someone ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I need you to keep me up to date while you're away. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le14ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about saving money for the future.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "safe and sound", "type": "name"}, {"content": "free from danger or injury", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm back home safe and sound!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le14ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "elusive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "hard to understand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You've been so elusive about your future. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le14ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "reasonable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "fairly or moderately good", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That sounds reasonable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le14ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to keep an eye on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bwatch someone or something or \u200bstay \u200binformed about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to keep an eye on your money.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le14ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "returns", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the monetary benefits one gets back from investing their money", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I just hope I'm getting the best returns on my investments.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le14ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to be ahead of the game", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have an advantage in a competitive situation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're ahead of the game.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le14ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to squirrel away", "type": "name"}, {"content": "save up for future use", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have friends who have already squirreled away enough savings to retire! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le14ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn9le14ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Think of 12 questions to ask someone about her/his future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the questions, making sure that you use various verb tenses (simple present, going to, present continuous, future continuous, future perfect and simple future).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find two people and ask them the questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes on their answers to each question.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I think of and write down 12 questions about the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask two people the questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I take notes on their answers.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn9le14ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn9le14ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Back home safe and sound!\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Let's grab a taxi.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Peter's picking us up soon. Oh, there he is! Peter!\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Hey girls! I'm glad you had a great trip. Glad you kept me up to date while you were away. Will you be heading back to work tomorrow?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yes, I'll be blogging!\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I am putting in at least 60 hours at the restaurant this week. If I can keep that up, I'll have paid for almost half my trip by the end of the month."}, {"image": "engenn9le14ob09re2img01.jpg", "time": "29000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I wish I could have gone with you guys but I have a plan.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: You've been so elusive about your future. What's your plan?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: In five years, I'll have saved enough money to buy a house. Before that happens I'll have started my own PR company. Basically for the next two years I am going to spend as little money as possible.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: That sounds reasonable. I will also stop squandering my money. It's going to be a challenge.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Money doesn't grow on trees! You have to keep an eye on your money."}, {"image": "engenn9le14ob09re2img02.jpg", "time": "60000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I am starting a retirement fund as soon as I pay off the trip. I meet with someone at the bank tomorrow. It opens at 8:30 and I have the first appointment.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Good idea. I just hope I'm getting the best returns on my investments.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: You guys will be fine. You're ahead of the game.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I don't know. I have friends who have already squirreled away enough savings to retire!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le14ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le14ob09re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about jobs, work and money.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about future action. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Are you someone who can easily save money for the future? Explain.", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Are people in your country able to save money for retirement? Why? Why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "How long will I be working?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " Vanessa, Peter and Sally <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">get serious</span> about the future!", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skil